#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:1
msgid "Hex Worlds and a Mini-Catan Board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:3
msgid ""
"This example combines 19 land tiles with settlements on vertices and "
"roads on edges. It builds on the [Hex Worlds "
"tutorial](../tutorial/hex_world.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:7
msgid "Build the island"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:9
msgid ""
"The grid is seven columns by seven rows. Only the positions listed in "
"`land_rows` belong to the island. The five land rows contain 3, 4, 5, 4, "
"and 3 tiles. Both even rows start at column 2, so they are centered "
"between the shifted odd rows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:14
msgid ""
"Each land tile stores a terrain name and a dice number. Its six corners "
"form the polygon that shows the terrain. The `land` dictionary also lets "
"the placement rules test whether a corner or edge touches the island."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:18
msgid "Place pieces on shared corners and edges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:20
msgid "Run the script below and use these controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:22
msgid ""
"Left-click near a land corner to place a settlement. The corner and its "
"immediate neighbors must be free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:24
msgid ""
"Right-click near an edge to place a road. The edge must touch land, have "
"a settlement at one end, and be free."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:26
msgid ""
"Press Space to distribute resources for a sample roll of 8. The center "
"tile has number 8. Place a settlement on one of its corners to see a gain"
" printed in the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:30
msgid ""
"A shared corner has one `.position`, even if you look it up from "
"different land tiles. The same applies to edges. The script uses these "
"positions as keys in `settlements` and `roads`, so both sides of a tile "
"boundary refer to the same piece."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:138
msgid "Follow a placement or resource payout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:140
msgid ""
"`get_neighbour_tiles()` on a corner or edge answers which existing tiles "
"touch it. `corner.get_neighbour_corners()` follows one edge in each "
"direction from the corner. `edge.get_neighbour_corners()` gives the two "
"endpoints. The script draws the road as a line between them. The full "
"board is visible here, so the endpoints' world pixels can be used "
"directly on the background. These queries work both in the middle of the "
"island and on its coast."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:148
msgid ""
"For a payout, the script starts from the tile that matches the roll and "
"visits its six corners with `tile.get_neighbour_corners()`. Each occupied"
" corner contributes one `(owner, terrain)` pair. For example, with one "
"settlement on the center tile the output is `Gains for roll 8: [('Red', "
"'hill')]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:154
msgid ""
"The example uses one player and a fixed roll so you can reproduce the "
"placement and payout. For a playable version, store the current player in"
" the piece dictionaries, apply ownership when checking connections, roll "
"two dice, and add the returned gains to inventories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/patterns/hex_world_catan.md:159
msgid ""
"The [HexWorld API reference](../api/world_hex.md) lists the other "
"adjacency methods, including the edges incident to a corner and the edges"
" that share an endpoint."
msgstr ""

